/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 125 0 R
/E (Thus, the experiments were successfully performed using JFLAP software to understand and implement different concepts of automata theory. The experiments demonstrated the construction and testing of Deterministic Finite Automata \(DFA\) and Non-Deterministic Finite Automata \(NFA\), conversion of NFA to DFA, DFA minimization, conversion of DFA into regular grammars and regular expressions, and the combination of automata to perform language operations. The conversion of regular expressions into finite automata was also explored. Additionally, Mealy and Moore machines were implemented to understand how finite-state machines generate outputs based on transitions and states, respectively. Overall, these experiments provided practical knowledge of finite- state machines, regular languages, and their applications using JFLAP. )
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
